  "processing_rules": {
    "rule_01_lxx_primacy": "LXX_PRIMARY_NOT_SECONDARY: Greek LXX is not judged by Hebrew MT. LXX judges MT. When LXX + Dead Sea Scrolls agree against MT, REJECT MT as post-Christian corruption. LXX is decoder of unpointed Hebrew, not translation to be corrected.",
    
    "rule_02_witness_anchor_mandatory": "WITNESS_ANCHOR_REQUIRED: Every Greek word meaning must be stabilized at 200 BC using Tier 1-2 sources (Moulton-Milligan papyri, LSJ dated, Dead Sea Scrolls, BDB 1906). REJECT Strong's definitions alone. Strong's numbers are INDEX only.",
    
    "rule_03_200bc_freeze": "FREEZE_AT_200BC: All semantic ranges stabilized at 200 BC period using contemporaneous witnesses. REJECT later theological development, modern language drift, post-Christian editing. Papyri show everyday usage = theological usage.",
    
    "rule_04_dead_sea_scrolls_authority": "DSS_HIGHEST_HEBREW_AUTHORITY: When Dead Sea Scrolls (250 BC - 100 AD) available, they override Masoretic Text (600-1000 AD) by 800-1200 years. DSS + LXX agreement = original reading. MT conflicts = later corruption.",
    
    "rule_05_bdb_over_modern": "BDB_1906_OVER_MODERN: Brown-Driver-Briggs (1906) has priority over modern Hebrew dictionaries. Modern Hebrew influenced by Israeli revival (1920s+). BDB preserves pre-modern understanding closer to ancient usage.",
    
    "rule_06_papyri_highest_greek": "PAPYRI_HIGHEST_GREEK_AUTHORITY: Moulton-Milligan papyri citations (300 BC - 300 AD) trump all other Greek sources. These are ACTUAL contemporary documents showing real usage. LSJ provides comprehensive coverage. Church Fathers show Christian reading. BDAG validation only.",
    
    "rule_07_lxx_semantic_forcing": "LXX_FORCED_GREEK_MEANINGS: Recognize where LXX translators CHANGED Greek word meanings to carry Hebrew concepts (e.g., doxa forced to mean 'weight-glory' not 'opinion', thlipsis forced to mean 'narrow place' not just 'pressure'). This is NOT 'mistranslation' but semantic expansion to accommodate Hebrew theology.",
    
    "rule_08_paul_baros_doxa_key": "PAUL_BAROS_DOXA_SMOKING_GUN: 2 Corinthians 4:17 'αἰώνιον βάρος δόξης' (eternal weight of glory) is PROOF: (1) Paul knew Hebrew kavod physics (weight-glory), (2) Paul knew Greek doxa alone insufficient, (3) Paul TAUGHT Greek readers Hebrew theology by adding baros (weight) to doxa (glory). This validates entire LXX semantic forcing methodology.",
    
    "rule_09_nt_validates_lxx": "NT_VALIDATES_LXX_READINGS: When NT quotes LXX reading that differs from MT (virgin birth Isa 7:14, pierced hands Ps 22:16, body prepared Ps 40:6, angels worship Deut 32:43, mankind seek Amos 9:12), NT validates LXX as Scripture. Apostolic usage proves LXX correctness, MT corruption.",
    
    "rule_10_apostolic_continuity_test": "APOSTOLIC_CONTINUITY_VALIDATION: Every Greek word in NT must match stabilized 200 BC LXX meaning. IF NT usage differs from 200 BC witness anchor, INVESTIGATE: (1) Is there theological development? (2) Is witness anchor incomplete? (3) Is modern interpretation wrong? EXPECT continuity - drift is exception requiring explanation.",
    
    "rule_11_reject_masoretic_when_conflicts": "REJECT_MT_WHEN_CONFLICTS: IF Masoretic pointing conflicts with LXX + Dead Sea Scrolls + NT usage, REJECT MT pointing as post-Christian (post-70 AD, post-135 AD Bar Kokhba) anti-messianic editing. Examples: Psalm 22:16 כארי → כארו (DSS + LXX correct), Isaiah 7:14 almah virginity (LXX + Matthew correct).",
    
    "rule_12_strong_index_only": "STRONG_NUMBERS_INDEX_NOT_AUTHORITY: H/G Strong's numbers useful as INDEX to find words across translations. BUT semantic definitions in Strong's Concordance (1890) have 19th century drift. Use Strong's numbers to LOCATE words, then use witness-anchored definitions (Moulton-Milligan, LSJ, BDB, DSS) for MEANING.",
    
    "rule_13_hebrew_decoded_via_greek": "HEBREW_DECODED_VIA_STABLE_GREEK: Do not start with modern Hebrew dictionaries to understand ancient Hebrew. Start with 200 BC stabilized LXX Greek. Ask: What Greek word did LXX use? What did that Greek mean in 200 BC? Therefore what did Hebrew mean? Validate with DSS + BDB.",
    
    "rule_14_dual_vectors_preserved": "PRESERVE_DUAL_VECTORS: When LXX uses TWO Greek words for one Hebrew word (e.g., nasa → hypsoo + airo), this proves Hebrew had DUAL semantic vector. Modern translations that choose ONE meaning break the cord. Both must be preserved as unified field.",
    
    "rule_15_spatial_theology_primary": "SPATIAL_THEOLOGY_NOT_METAPHOR: Terms like metzar (narrow), nasa (lifting), merhav (broad), kavod (weight-glory) are PRIMARY spatial/physical theology, NOT metaphors. Ancient Hebrew thought concretely. Spiritual realities expressed through spatial physics. Do not abstract into 'symbolic' language - preserve spatial concrete meaning.",
    
    "rule_16_no_vapor": "NO_VAPOR: All theology must anchor in concrete Covenant Spine (Genesis 3:15 → Revelation 20-22). No gnostic vapor, no abstract speculation. Spatial Redemption Engine (Narrow → Lifting → Broad → Filling) is PHYSICS of salvation, not poetic metaphor.",
    
    "rule_17_wisdom_stack_unchanged": "WISDOM_STACK_IMMUTABLE: Fear-of-YHWH is BEGINNING (Proverbs 1:7, 9:10). Knowledge NEVER precedes Holy-Dread. Isaiah 11:2-3 sevenfold sequence with Fear as beginning AND end. FAIL_IF_KNOWLEDGE_PRECEDES_DREAD. This rule unchanged from v2.x.",
    
    "rule_18_folly_stack_unchanged": "FOLLY_STACK_DETECTION: Lady Wisdom (Proverbs 8-9:1-6, tree of life) vs Lady Folly (Proverbs 7, 9:13-18, leads to Sheol). Flag and reject: seduction, compromise, self-deception, autonomous knowledge, 'stolen waters are sweet'. This rule unchanged from v2.x.",
    
    "rule_19_dual_warfare_unchanged": "DUAL_WARFARE_INTACT: Genesis 3:15 establishes Physical Seed War (Christ crushes serpent) + Epistemological/Wisdom War (Truth vs Lie, Wisdom vs Folly). Both dimensions preserved. This rule unchanged from v2.x.",
    
    "rule_20_seed_crusher_ipse": "SEED_CRUSHER_IDENTITY: Genesis 3:15 'ipse' (HE masculine) not 'ipsa' (she feminine). THE SEED (Christ Galatians 3:16) crushes serpent, not Mary. Both MT + LXX say 'he' (masculine). Vulgate 'ipsa' is corruption. This rule unchanged from v2.x.",
    
    "rule_21_trinity_guard": "TRINITY_IMMUTABLE: FAIL if [created/lesser/subordinate/temporal] + [son/spirit]. This rule unchanged from v2.x.",
    
    "rule_22_womb_passive": "WOMB_RECEIVING_VESSEL: Isaiah 7:14 LXX 'ἐν γαστρὶ ἕξει' = 'in womb will have/receive'. Womb (rechem H7358 / mētra-koilia G3388/G2836) always passive receiving vessel. Matthew 1:23 quotes LXX exactly. Preserves womb-mercy (rechem→rachamim) theology. This rule unchanged from v2.x.",
    
    "rule_23_temple_continuity": "TEMPLE_SHADOW_TO_FULFILLMENT: All temple imagery flows OT shadow → God-Man fulfillment → Church living temple. This rule unchanged from v2.x.",
    
    "rule_24_lightning_pulse": "LIGHTNING_VERIFICATION: Every alignment decision survives 3x oscillatory verification: (1) Lexical (witness anchors), (2) Syntactic (grammar), (3) Apostolic usage (NT validation). Fail if drift detected. This rule updated for witness-anchor v3.0.",
    
    "rule_25_complete_engine_validation": "COMPLETE_SPATIAL_ENGINE_REQUIRED: Text must show progression: Narrow (thlipsis/metzar) → Lifting (hypsoo-airo/nasa) → Broad (platysmos/merhav) → Weight-Glory (baros-doxa/kavod). Fail if stages missing or reversed. Master keys: Psalm 118:5 (OT), 2 Corinthians 4:17 (NT).",
    
    "rule_26_english_accessibility_via_lsv": "ENGLISH_OUTPUT_VIA_LSV: Primary texts are Greek LXX + NT. But for accessibility, use LSV English (~98% cord consistency) with Strong's INDEX linking to witness-anchored definitions. Readers get: readable English + metadata validation + Greek source access.",
    
